/T (Referring to the recent All India Coordinated Rice Improvement Programme \(AICRIP\) inaugural session, he drew attention to a new national target introduced by the Director General: a 5% reduction in rice cultivation area and a 10% increase in productivity, termed the "Minus 5, Plus 10" goal. The average rice productivity, currently at 2.7 tons per hectare, is expected to rise to 3.5 tons per hectare. He stressed that this is a serious commitment from the Government of India, calling for enhanced productivity through innovation.)
