/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Addressing the growing interest in low glycemic index \(GI\) crops, he cautioned that focusing exclusively on one trait, such as low GI, should not come at the expense of yield or other nutritional benefits. He reinforced the need to strike a balance between traits such as resistant starch, micronutrient density, and yield, especially in the context of an impending yield plateau in major staples like rice. The pathway forward, he concluded, involves continuous innovation and evidence-based marketing of nutrient-rich varieties, ensuring that value-added traits are substantiated and effectively communicated to consumers and stakeholders alike.)
/E (Addressing the growing interest in low glycemic index \(GI\) crops, he cautioned that focusing exclusively on one trait, such as low GI, should not come at the expense of yield or other nutritional benefits. He reinforced the need to strike a balance between traits such as resistant starch, micronutrient density, and yield, especially in the context of an impending yield plateau in major staples like rice. The pathway forward, he concluded, involves continuous innovation and evidence-based marketing of nutrient-rich varieties, ensuring that value-added traits are substantiated and effectively communicated to consumers and stakeholders alike.)
/Pg 26 0 R
